title: Payers › Process › Read the workflow
route: /payers/summit?tab=process
intro: The Process tab shows how an authorization works with one payer: numbered steps in order, with the condition drawn next to the step it leads to. The step-type key and the note about edits sit behind an info icon. How the payer is reached and the script for Caller are folded into one closed section. A banner shows only when edits or proposals wait.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click the 'Process' tab\n(the tab shown when none is named)"
screen tab "Process tab\nBanners, workflow card, one closed section"

group gB "Banners at the top (only when they apply)"
  decision dU "Edits saved but\nnot yet applied to open drafts?"
  toast bU "'1 edit applies to new drafts only'\nNew drafts for Summit use this at once.\nSent requests keep what they were sent with.\nClick Update drafts to redraft the open ones (R-1042, R-1101)."
  decision dP "Did Historian propose changes?"
  toast bP "'Historian proposed 1 change'\nIt never edits the workflow on its own.\n'Review in Changes'"
endgroup

screen card "Workflow card\n'How an authorization works with Summit' with an info icon\n'Version 7, edited 10/12.'\n'Edit workflow' and 'Re-learn from decisions'"
click cTip "Hover, focus or click the info icon\n(button 'About this workflow')"
overlay tip "Info tip\nThe workflow in order, where the path splits\nThe key: Checklist step, File step, Portal step, Phone step, Condition\n'Admins can edit; every edit is logged. New drafts use a saved edit at once.\nSent requests keep what they were sent with. Click Update drafts to redraft open ones.'\nEscape closes it"

group gS "One numbered step"
  screen st "Number, step title, step-type chip, agent chips\nFor example: 'Give notice'  Portal step  Navigator"
  process stx "Plain sentence on what happens\nand a 'Typical' time on the right\n'same day', '2 minutes', '1.5 days'"
  decision dc "Does the step have conditions?"
  screen br "Condition rows under the step\n'If portal is down' leads to\n'Phone step' and what happens"
endgroup

process six "Summit's six steps: Check coverage,\nGather the documents, Give notice,\nSend the request, Follow up,\nDecision and next review"
process diff "Other payers differ in how they are reached\nEvergreen: phone steps\nLakeshore: file steps by fax\nHarborview: portal with fax for large files"
screen two "Closed section\n'How to reach Summit and what Caller says'\n'Reached by portal, phone as backup. Caller script saved 10/12.'\nOpens to 'How to reach Summit' and 'Instructions for Caller' side by side"

click cE "Click 'Edit workflow'"
click cR "Click 'Re-learn from decisions'"
click cRev "Click 'Review in Changes'"
click cUp "Click 'Update 2 drafts'"
goto g_ed "Continues in: Payers › Process › Edit the workflow"
goto g_rl "Continues in: Payers › Process › Re-learn from decisions"
goto g_ch "Continues in: Payers › Changes › Read what changed"
goto g_up "Continues in: Payers › Edits waiting › Update drafts"
goto g_rc "Continues in: Payers › Process › Reach and Caller instructions"

s1 --> tab --> dU
dU -->|Yes| bU --> dP
dU -->|No| dP
dP -->|Yes| bP --> card
dP -->|No| card
card --> st --> stx --> dc
card -.-> cTip --> tip
dc -->|Yes| br
dc -->|No| six
br --> six
six -.-> diff
six --> two
card --> cE --> g_ed
card --> cR --> g_rl
bP --> cRev --> g_ch
bU --> cUp --> g_up
two -.-> g_rc
